{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAParentalGate"},"kind":"article","metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"role":"article","title":"Add a Parental Gate"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginParentalGateReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture"],"anchor":"Related-Documentation","title":"Related Documentation"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAPaywall","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAVersionKillswitch","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAnalytics","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddFeatureFlags","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToCancelEffects","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddPersistence","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddICloudSync","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingADomainPlugin","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/AgentSkill"],"generated":true,"anchor":"How-to-Guides","title":"How-to Guides"}],"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Gate sensitive actions — purchases, settings changes, leaving a kid-mode area — behind a math challenge."}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"],["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SecurityPosture"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"When you finish, your app will:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Hold a ","type":"text"},{"code":"ParentalGateState","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" slice in ","type":"text"},{"code":"AppState","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and a ","type":"text"},{"code":"parentalGate","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" action case in ","type":"text"},{"code":"AppAction","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Run ","type":"text"},{"code":"ParentalGatePlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" as part of the store’s plugin host.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Present a math-challenge sheet whenever a feature requests a gate, and resume the original action once the user solves it.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For the API surface, see "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginParentalGateReference"},{"type":"text","text":". For how domain plugins fit into the dispatch lifecycle, see "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Before you start","anchor":"Before-you-start"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"This guide assumes you already have a Swidux app wired with ","type":"text"},{"code":"AppState","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"AppAction","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", an ","type":"text"},{"code":"AppReducer","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Store.configured()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" factory. If you don’t, start with the getting-started material and come back here.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Step 1: Add the dependency","anchor":"Step-1-Add-the-dependency"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The parental-gate plugin ships as a separate library product. Add it to your target’s dependencies:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["\/\/ Package.swift",".target(","    name: \"MyApp\",","    dependencies: [","        .product(name: \"Swidux\", package: \"Swidux\"),","        .product(name: \"SwiduxParentalGate\", package: \"Swidux\"),","    ]",")"]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Step 2: Add state and actions","anchor":"Step-2-Add-state-and-actions"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Nest a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ParentalGateState"},{"type":"text","text":" slice on your root state, and add an action case that wraps "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ParentalGateAction"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["\/\/ AppState.swift","import SwiduxParentalGate","","@Swidux","nonisolated struct AppState: Equatable, Sendable {","    @Slice var parentalGate: ParentalGateState = .init()","    \/\/ … other slices","}","","\/\/ AppAction.swift","enum AppAction: Sendable {","    case parentalGate(ParentalGateAction)","    \/\/ … other cases","}"]},{"name":"Tip","type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import SwiduxParentalGate"},{"type":"text","text":" is needed in "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"every","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" file that touches ","type":"text"},{"code":"store.parentalGate.*","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"ParentalGateAction","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — including views that read the slice for display. ","type":"text"},{"code":"@_exported import Swidux","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" re-exports core Swidux only, not plugin modules. See ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}],"style":"tip"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The plugin owns the parental-gate slice end-to-end, so the root reducer just falls through:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["\/\/ AppReducer.swift","case .parentalGate:","    return nil"],"type":"codeListing"},{"level":2,"text":"Step 3: Wire the plugin","anchor":"Step-3-Wire-the-plugin","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Construct ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ParentalGatePlugin"},{"text":" inside ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Store.configured()"},{"text":" and register it with the plugin host. Use ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ParentalChallengeSource.standard"},{"text":" for production:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["\/\/ AppStore.swift","let parentalGatePlugin = ParentalGatePlugin<AppState, AppAction>(","    state: \\.parentalGate,","    action: AppAction.parentalGate,","    extractAction: { if case .parentalGate(let a) = $0 { return a }; return nil },","    challengeSource: .standard",")","","let plugins = PluginHost<AppState, AppAction>()","plugins.register(undoPlugin)","plugins.register(persistencePlugin)","plugins.register(parentalGatePlugin)"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Domain plugins use only the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce"},{"type":"text","text":" hook, so registration order relative to other domain plugins rarely matters."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"After three wrong answers in a row ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"attemptLimit:"},{"type":"text","text":") the gate refuses every answer for 30 seconds ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cooldown:"},{"type":"text","text":"). As wired above, that limit lives in memory, so it is "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"per process"}]},{"text":": a child who force-quits the app from the switcher gets a fresh set of guesses on relaunch. To make it survive, give the plugin a ","type":"text"},{"code":"KeyValueStore","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and hydrate the slice from the same store:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["\/\/ AppStore.swift","let kv = UserDefaultsKeyValueStore()","let parentalGatePlugin = ParentalGatePlugin<AppState, AppAction>(","    state: \\.parentalGate,","    action: AppAction.parentalGate,","    extractAction: { if case .parentalGate(let a) = $0 { return a }; return nil },","    challengeSource: .standard,","    keyValueStore: kv",")","","var initialState = AppState()","initialState.parentalGate = .hydrated(from: kv)"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Only the attempt count and the cooldown deadline are stored; "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"passedReasons"},{"text":" still resets every launch.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Step-4-Gate-an-action","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Step 4: Gate an action"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Pick a stable reason key per gated action (for example "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"purchase\""},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"settings\""},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"exit-kid-mode\""},{"type":"text","text":"). In a view or feature reducer, check "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"passedReasons"},{"type":"text","text":" before performing the work:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["Button(\"Buy gems\") {","    if store.parentalGate.passedReasons.contains(\"purchase\") {","        store.send(.shop(.buyGems))","    } else {","        store.send(.parentalGate(.request(reason: \"purchase\")))","    }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To resume the original action automatically once the user solves the challenge, listen for "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".answerAccepted(reason:)"},{"text":" in the relevant feature reducer and re-dispatch:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["\/\/ ShopReducer.swift","func reduce(","    state: inout AppState,","    action: AppAction,","    environment: AppEnvironment",") -> Effect? {","    switch action {","    case .parentalGate(.answerAccepted(let reason)) where reason == \"purchase\":","        return Effect { send in await send(.shop(.buyGems)) }","    \/\/ …","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"This pattern keeps the gate logic local to the feature it protects: the gate just emits ","type":"text"},{"code":"answerAccepted","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and each feature decides what — if anything — to resume."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Step-5-Present-the-challenge-sheet","level":2,"text":"Step 5: Present the challenge sheet"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Drive sheet presentation off "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"pendingReason"},{"text":". Bind text input to a local ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":" for the typed answer, dispatch "},{"code":"ParentalGateAction.submitAnswer(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" on confirm, and "},{"code":"ParentalGateAction.regenerateChallenge","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for a “new question” button.","type":"text"}]},{"code":["struct ContentView: View {","    @Environment(AppStore.self) private var store","","    var body: some View {","        \/\/ … your app UI","            .sheet(isPresented: Binding(","                get: { store.parentalGate.pendingReason != nil },","                set: { if !$0 { store.send(.parentalGate(.dismiss)) } }","            )) {","                ParentalGateSheet()","            }","    }","}","","struct ParentalGateSheet: View {","    @Environment(AppStore.self) private var store","    @State private var answer: String = \"\"","","    var body: some View {","        VStack(spacing: 16) {","            if let challenge = store.parentalGate.challenge {","                Text(\"\\(challenge.left) \\(challenge.op.symbol) \\(challenge.right) = ?\")","                    .font(.title)","","                TextField(\"Answer\", text: $answer)","                    .keyboardType(.numberPad)","","                if let until = store.parentalGate.cooldownUntil {","                    Text(\"Too many wrong answers. Try again in \\(Text(until, style: .timer)).\")","                        .foregroundStyle(.secondary)","                }","","                HStack {","                    Button(\"New question\") {","                        store.send(.parentalGate(.regenerateChallenge))","                        answer = \"\"","                    }","                    Button(\"Submit\") {","                        if let value = Int(answer) {","                            store.send(.parentalGate(.submitAnswer(value)))","                        }","                        answer = \"\"","                    }","                    .disabled(store.parentalGate.cooldownUntil != nil)","                }","            }","        }","        .padding()","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"When the user submits a wrong answer, the plugin increments ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"attempts"},{"text":" and regenerates the challenge automatically, so the sheet just re-renders with the new operands.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"At the attempt limit the plugin sets ","type":"text"},{"code":"cooldownUntil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and refuses every answer, correct ones included, until it dispatches ","type":"text"},{"code":".cooldownExpired","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and clears it. Disabling Submit while ","type":"text"},{"code":"cooldownUntil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is non-"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":" makes that visible instead of silently swallowing the answer. It can’t strand the sheet: the plugin arms the expiry when the limit is reached and re-arms it on every "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".request"},{"type":"text","text":" during a cooldown, so dismissing and reopening the gate always brings "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".cooldownExpired"},{"type":"text","text":" — including after a relaunch that hydrated a cooldown, or after the scene’s effects were cancelled. The expiry follows the monotonic clock, so if the user changes the device clock the countdown text can read early or late, but the cooldown itself neither ends early nor runs long."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Reasons that should be passed once vs. always re-challenged","level":2,"anchor":"Reasons-that-should-be-passed-once-vs-always-re-challenged"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The auto-pass behavior of ","type":"text"},{"code":"ParentalGateAction.request(reason:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (see "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginParentalGateReference","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":") is a design choice: once a reason is in ","type":"text"},{"code":"passedReasons","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", future ","type":"text"},{"code":".request","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" calls for it short-circuit. That’s the right default for low-stakes gates inside a single session — the user shouldn’t solve the same problem every time they tap the same button."}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"For higher-stakes gates that should always re-challenge, use a fresh reason key each time:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["store.send(.parentalGate(.request(reason: \"purchase-\\(UUID().uuidString)\")))"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Or, more usefully, clear the relevant entries from "},{"code":"passedReasons","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" at meaningful boundaries — app launch, session timeout, or returning from background. Mutate the set directly from your own reducer:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["case .app(.didEnterBackground):","    state.parentalGate.passedReasons.removeAll()","    return nil"]},{"anchor":"Testing","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Testing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For deterministic tests, swap the standard generator for "},{"code":"ParentalChallengeSource.fixed(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":":","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["@MainActor","@Test func correctAnswerAcceptsAndPasses() async throws {","    let challenge = MathChallenge(left: 2, right: 3, op: .plus)  \/\/ expected = 5","    let plugin = ParentalGatePlugin<AppState, AppAction>(","        state: \\.parentalGate,","        action: AppAction.parentalGate,","        extractAction: { if case .parentalGate(let a) = $0 { return a }; return nil },","        challengeSource: .fixed(challenge)","    )","","    var state = AppState()","    state.parentalGate.pendingReason = \"settings\"","    state.parentalGate.challenge = challenge","","    let effect = try #require(","        plugin.reduce(state: &state, action: .parentalGate(.submitAnswer(5)))","    )","","    var dispatched: [AppAction] = []","    try await effect { dispatched.append($0) }","","    if case .parentalGate(.answerAccepted(let reason)) = dispatched.first {","        #expect(reason == \"settings\")","    } else {","        Issue.record(\"expected answerAccepted, got \\(dispatched)\")","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxParentalGateTests"},{"type":"text","text":" target in this package uses the same pattern — a fixed challenge plus a small test root state — and is a good reference when wiring tests for your own gated features."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddaparentalgate"]}],"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddAPaywall":{"role":"article","title":"Add a Paywall","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddapaywall","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAPaywall","kind":"article","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Wire the ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxPaywall","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" plugin into a Swidux app to gate features behind a subscription or lifetime purchase.","type":"text"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddAVersionKillswitch":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAVersionKillswitch","kind":"article","title":"Add a Version Killswitch","role":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Wire a remote-controlled blocker that covers the UI of unsupported app versions, with an “Update” path back to the App Store.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddaversionkillswitch"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginParentalGateReference":{"kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"API surface for the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxParentalGate"},{"type":"text","text":" library — a domain plugin that guards actions behind a math challenge."}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginparentalgatereference","type":"topic","role":"article","title":"SwiduxParentalGate Reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginParentalGateReference"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","role":"collection","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Redux-style state management for SwiftUI, with macros for observability and ready-made plugins for persistence, undo, paywalls, version killswitches, and parental gates."}],"title":"Swidux","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swidux"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddICloudSync":{"kind":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Layer opt-in, cross-device iCloud sync on top of ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxPersistence","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with the ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxCloudKitSync","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" plugin — including a runtime opt-out toggle, launch-time entitlement detection, and the Apple Developer portal configuration.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddicloudsync","type":"topic","role":"article","title":"Add iCloud Sync","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddICloudSync"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/SecurityPosture":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/securityposture","kind":"article","title":"Security Posture","abstract":[{"text":"What Swidux’s soft controls actually guarantee, and what to do when you need a hard one.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SecurityPosture","role":"collectionGroup"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/AgentSkill":{"kind":"article","role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Install the bundled "},{"code":"swidux-ref","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" skill so your AI coding assistant has Swidux’s architecture rules and code templates on hand."}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/agentskill","title":"Using the Swidux Agent Skill","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/AgentSkill","type":"topic"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginArchitecture":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","title":"Plugin Architecture","role":"article","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginarchitecture","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Extend the dispatch cycle with lifecycle hooks — from invisible infrastructure to domain-specific features."}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddAnalytics":{"role":"article","title":"Add Analytics","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddanalytics","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAnalytics","kind":"article","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Wire the ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxAnalytics","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" plugin into a Swidux app for centralized event tracking with declarative event mapping and auto-identify.","type":"text"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddPersistence":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddPersistence","role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Persist your domain entities to SwiftData with the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxPersistence"},{"type":"text","text":" plugin and the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Persisted"},{"type":"text","text":" macro — no hand-written "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Model"},{"type":"text","text":" classes, database actors, or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"StateWriter"},{"type":"text","text":" closures."}],"title":"Add Persistence","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddpersistence","kind":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToCancelEffects":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToCancelEffects","kind":"article","title":"Cancel Effects","role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Tag an effect with an identity so it can be cancelled later — by another effect, or imperatively from view code."}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtocanceleffects"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/BuildingADomainPlugin":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingADomainPlugin","kind":"article","title":"Building a Domain Plugin","role":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Create a self-contained feature plugin with its own state, actions, and effects.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/buildingadomainplugin"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddFeatureFlags":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddFeatureFlags","title":"Add Feature Flags","role":"article","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddfeatureflags","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Wire the "},{"code":"SwiduxFeatureFlags","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" plugin into a Swidux app for typed feature flags, A\/B variants, and remote-tunable scalar values from a single JSON config.","type":"text"}]}}}